# Line endings (2026-11-02, docs/claude/2026-11-02-legacy-cleanup.md).
# Default: text is stored and checked out with LF on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf says. This keeps
# pinned source hashes (scripts/*-discovery.mjs, smoke harness) identical on a Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Preserve reviewed upstream bytes so source ZIPs match the pinned asset hashes.
assets/bundled/** -text
# Windows launchers keep CRLF regardless of checkout settings.
*.cmd -text

# Files committed with CRLF or mixed line endings keep their exact bytes. "-text" (not "eol=crlf") on purpose:
# eol=crlf would store LF in the index, so `git add --renormalize .` would rewrite them, and a mixed file has no
# single eol to declare. electron/codex.ts is pinned by hash (scripts/lib/smoke-isolation.mjs LOCATOR_SHA256).
# To convert one to LF, do it in its own commit and remove its line here.
